book.summary.title=Contents

book.guide.introduction.title=Welcome, Evoker
book.guide.introduction.text=The Evoke Book brings Hex objects to life.\n\nSome blocks are Hex items: when evoked, they turn into Hex Creatures that follow you and help with everyday tasks, such as harvesting crops, storing items in chests or lighting the way.\n\nThis book has three bookmarks:\n- My Creatures: the Hex Creatures you have evoked\n- Evoke Book: tips and an introduction to the mod\n- Hex Creatures: a page for each creature, with its origin item, cost, upkeep and characteristics
book.guide.evoking.title=Evoking
book.guide.evoking.text=Place a Hex item, stand close to it (up to 3 blocks away) and use the primary action of the Evoke Book. The nearest Hex item comes to life.\n\nYou can have up to 6 Hex Creatures at the same time.\n\nWhat is stored in the block goes with the creature: the contents of a chest go to the Chest Spider's inventory, and the armor and weapon of a Hex Mannequin are equipped on the creature.
book.guide.life_essence.title=Essence of Life
book.guide.life_essence.text=Evoking a Hex Creature costs Essence of Life. The cost is taken from your inventory at the moment of the evocation; if you do not have enough, nothing happens.\n\nThe Essence of Life spent is kept inside the creature (see Essence Storage). The cost of each creature is shown in the Hex Creatures bookmark.\n\nHex items do not use Essence of Life in their recipes: it is only paid when evoking. Look for the Hex items in the Hexcode Evoke category at the Arcane Bench and at the Alchemy Bench.
book.guide.essence_storage.title=Essence Storage
book.guide.essence_storage.text=Every Hex Creature stores the Essence of Life used to evoke it. The storage starts full, and its limit is the evocation cost.\n\nSome creatures spend this Essence over time. The upkeep per minute is shown in the Hex Creatures bookmark, and how much is left is shown in My Creatures. Essence is only spent while the creature is loaded in the world.\n\nIf the creature carries Essence of Life anywhere in its inventory, it refills itself whenever at least 1 whole unit is missing. Creatures with upkeep also pick up Essence of Life dropped on the ground nearby and keep it in their inventory instead of storing it in chests.\n\nYou are warned when a creature is running low. When the storage reaches zero, the creature turns back into its origin block and no Essence is returned; if there is no room for the block, it drops as an item.\n\nWhen you despawn or revert a creature, the Essence left in its storage (whole units only) drops where it was. If the creature dies, the Essence is lost.
book.guide.wands.title=Evoke Wands
book.guide.wands.text=Wands give orders to your Hex Creatures.\n\n- Primary: select a creature, or send the selected creatures to a location, where they stay\n- Charged Primary: select all creatures\n- Secondary: deselect a creature, or make the selected creatures follow you\n- Charged Secondary: deselect all creatures\n\nEach wand has a limit of selected creatures and a reach:\n- Crude Evoke Wand: 1 creature, 10 blocks\n- Wooden Evoke Wand: 3 creatures, 20 blocks\n- Iron Evoke Wand: 6 creatures, 30 blocks
book.guide.behaviour.title=Behaviour
book.guide.behaviour.text=By default, Hex Creatures follow you. When sent to a location with a wand, they stay there and start working: the Hex Broom wanders around collecting items, the Arcane Codex explores the chests nearby, and so on.\n\nIf you get too far away, most creatures teleport back to you.\n\nCreatures that work with items always look for the nearest chest, so keep chests close to where they work.
book.guide.managing.title=My Creatures
book.guide.managing.text=The My Creatures bookmark shows all your Hex Creatures and how many you have out of 6.\n\n- Essence of Life: how much is left in the creature's storage and, for creatures with upkeep, how long it lasts\n- Pencil: edit the names of the creatures; press Save to confirm\n- Checkbox: shows the name above the creature\n- Despawn: removes the creature, dropping its Hex item, its inventory and the Essence of Life left in its storage
book.guide.reverting.title=Reverting
book.guide.reverting.text=Look at one of your Hex Creatures and use the primary action of the Evoke Book to turn it back into its block, right where it stands.\n\nThe equipment of a Hex Mannequin goes back to the mannequin, and the inventory of a Chest Spider goes back to the chest. The Essence of Life left in the creature's storage drops on the ground.\n\nThe block needs free space under the creature.
book.guide.tips.title=Tips
book.guide.tips.text=- Interact with the creatures that carry items (Hex Mannequin, Homunculus, Chest Spider and Hex Broom) to open their profile, with equipment and inventory.\n- The other creatures can be put away by their owner by crouching and interacting with them.\n- The Hex Mannequin's job depends on the item in its hand.\n- The Chest Spider sorts the items you put in its inventory into your chests.\n- Send the Arcane Codex close to your chests and interact with it to find an item.

